01:23:08,555 --> 01:23:11,618
Confused me for a few seconds, but now we've moved on to the Venezuelan.

1354
01:23:11,639 --> 01:23:21,710
So Stephen Feck, who failed the dive, obviously suffered a bit of an injury when he slipped off the diving board in dramatic fashion and he's at the Venezuelan there back two and a half in the pike position.

1355
01:23:22,411 --> 01:23:23,431
Pretty middle of the road.

1356
01:23:23,872 --> 01:23:26,975
Sevens, but he's still performing consistently.

1357
01:23:27,076 --> 01:23:27,976
It's only twenty one.

1358
01:23:31,989 --> 01:23:33,572
Marks are as follows.

1359
01:23:34,052 --> 01:23:37,979
All the lines through those marks do not count, so the sevens all do.

1360
01:23:38,019 --> 01:23:40,481
And we have sixty-three.

1361
01:23:42,626 --> 01:23:47,792
Just to confirm for you, to confuse me for a bit as well, that seven feck is no longer in this competition.

1362
01:23:48,514 --> 01:23:53,761
He's gone but Cesar Castro very much in it with his back two and a half somersaults, twelfth after round three.

1363
01:23:55,750 --> 01:23:56,029
Yep.

1364
01:23:56,050 --> 01:23:57,652
It's okay from the Cesar.

1365
01:23:57,731 --> 01:23:59,354
This is lowest degree of difficulty.

1366
01:23:59,694 --> 01:24:00,636
So it needed to be good.

1367
01:24:00,655 --> 01:24:00,916
3.0.

1368
01:24:01,055 --> 01:24:04,279
It's got a couple of low DDs in there as we call them.

1369
01:24:04,980 --> 01:24:05,822
And this is one of them.

1370
01:24:06,382 --> 01:24:08,265
A couple more to follow actually.

1371
01:24:08,284 --> 01:24:16,855
Finishing his list with his, all of his dives, a little bit basic, which always makes it difficult for him to get in unless of course he's diving consistently, which he is.

1372
01:24:17,055 --> 01:24:22,061
I expect him to continue to do that and to sneak through into the semi-final.

1373
01:24:22,042 --> 01:24:42,530
yeah more than sinking at the moment but there's plenty of divers still to go third place for him now Keniyo of Malaysia he's having a good day and 11th after round three oh he continues to have a good day and this is what it's all about dive after dive consistency you can see lots of divers faltering

1374
01:24:42,511 --> 01:24:53,698
And the divers who are the ones who continue to focus on the job continue to land upright on their heads just like Kenny's doing there for us.

1375
01:24:54,801 --> 01:24:56,784
High 70s for that diver I would imagine.

1376
01:24:56,805 --> 01:24:58,951
3.3 degree of difficulty.

1377
01:24:59,372 --> 01:25:00,333
Good work Kenny.

1378
01:25:00,314 --> 01:25:05,261
Well, I've got to say, 71 followed by an 81, followed by a 72, followed by a 79.20.

1379
01:25:05,882 --> 01:25:12,112
We've had some consistent performers in the competition so far and he's certainly up there amongst them.

1380
01:25:13,293 --> 01:25:22,287
Patrick Housding, comfortable top ten at the moment, in with three and a half somersaults with Tuck, 3.4 for the only German now remaining in the competition.

1381
01:25:23,820 --> 01:25:28,409
Oh, precise, steady, unfaltering, and unwavering.

1382
01:25:29,332 --> 01:25:32,077
Big dive for Patrick, 3.4.

1383
01:25:32,998 --> 01:25:37,807
He's quite tall for a diver, so he needs to get his technique spot on, and he does just that.

1384
01:25:38,409 --> 01:25:41,154
Moving a safe, safe distance from the diving board.

1385
01:25:42,822 --> 01:25:44,805
Maybe a little bit too far away actually.

1386
01:25:44,985 --> 01:25:47,649
Struggled a little bit with his entry into the water.

1387
01:25:48,011 --> 01:25:50,835
If he gets a bit nearer and a bit higher he could get nines.

1388
01:25:51,176 --> 01:25:52,398
Seven and a half so for that one.

1389
01:25:52,417 --> 01:25:58,467
78.20 the total mark goes over the 300 points for Patrick Housding.

1390
01:25:59,528 --> 01:26:02,295
Alexei Pigorov started with a very high dive.

1391
01:26:02,314 --> 01:26:03,717
This is a high tariff of two.

1392
01:26:03,738 --> 01:26:05,662
3.5 on the reverse, three and a half somersaults.

1393
01:26:07,466 --> 01:26:10,975
Pigorov almost crashing out of the semi-finals there.

1394
01:26:12,158 --> 01:26:13,541
He did a great job though in the end.

1395
01:26:13,962 --> 01:26:15,225
Let's have a look at this takeoff.

1396
01:26:15,306 --> 01:26:16,569
Yeah, just skips forward.

1397
01:26:16,970 --> 01:26:18,030
I don't know whether you see that.

1398
01:26:18,091 --> 01:26:23,079
Skipping off at the knees and the hips and hangs on for dear life and just about sneaks.

1399
01:26:23,119 --> 01:26:24,121
And that is sneaky.

1400
01:26:24,402 --> 01:26:25,684
That must have hurt his back.

1401
01:26:25,703 --> 01:26:27,206
Yeah, that'll definitely jar his back.

1402
01:26:27,246 --> 01:26:33,777
But as divers, we're used to being beaten up by the gym and the water and occasionally after the competitors.

1403
01:26:33,796 --> 01:26:35,539
Just the way he adjusted his body when he was going in there.

1404
01:26:35,880 --> 01:26:38,925
You know, he feels like snapping his spine the way he went in like that.

1405
01:26:38,944 --> 01:26:42,411
Yeah, you just need to be tough when you're a diver.

1406
01:26:42,761 --> 01:26:46,466
Reverse three and a half somersaults for Garcia of Spain.

1407
01:26:47,868 --> 01:26:49,250
Oh, better effort there from Javi.

1408
01:26:49,310 --> 01:26:51,432
Needed a big one and a good one to get it in.

1409
01:26:52,134 --> 01:26:54,756
And that's certainly what he's done with his fourth fourth round.

1410
01:26:54,777 --> 01:26:56,298
A reverse three and a half.

1411
01:26:56,338 --> 01:26:57,119
It's a big dive.

1412
01:26:58,280 --> 01:26:59,141
Squeezing in.

1413
01:26:59,382 --> 01:27:00,604
Beautiful elevation.

1414
01:27:00,925 --> 01:27:04,048
Pops his feet up and slips into the water.

1415
01:27:04,729 --> 01:27:05,871
Without much of a trace.

1416
01:27:06,511 --> 01:27:11,637
Seventy-eight points.

1417
01:27:12,952 --> 01:27:15,136
Time to work out what the Canadian coach is doing.

1418
01:27:15,235 --> 01:27:17,019
Why is he clapping that when he's Spanish?

1419
01:27:17,560 --> 01:27:18,201
Oh, I didn't notice.

1420
01:27:18,261 --> 01:27:18,782
I'm sorry.

1421
01:27:18,801 --> 01:27:22,268
I was hoping that I got my points prediction correct, which I did.

1422
01:27:22,488 --> 01:27:24,351
We might even pay you at the end of the week if you're lucky.

1423
01:27:25,594 --> 01:27:28,359
Chris Colwell, reverse one and a half somersault, three and a half twist.

1424
01:27:28,378 --> 01:27:29,921
I think it's the first time we've seen this dive.

1425
01:27:29,942 --> 01:27:33,988
3.4 is the degree of difficulty in the free position.

1426
01:27:34,088 --> 01:27:35,972
Again, we haven't seen a free dive.

1427
01:27:35,993 --> 01:27:37,255
You can explain that after we've seen it.

1428
01:27:39,175 --> 01:28:07,292
It's very much a classic dive for any multiple twisting dive less than one and a half somersaults or one and a half somersaults or or less it is in the free position because you don't hold a position a pike or tuck for longer than half a rotation so it just squares it up nicely in the end 3.4 degree of difficulty you don't see I think you might be the only competitor choosing to use this one and a game of tactics working for Colwell there 3.4 it's a good dive

1429
01:28:08,335 --> 01:28:08,676
Yeah.

1430
01:28:09,056 --> 01:28:10,460
What do the judges think?

1431
01:28:10,479 --> 01:28:11,563
New set of judges, of course.

1432
01:28:11,662 --> 01:28:13,568
They've gone with the eights.

1433
01:28:13,587 --> 01:28:14,310
81.4.

1434
01:28:14,650 --> 01:28:16,154
Hang on a second, matey.

1435
01:28:16,175 --> 01:28:16,836
Rosset is gone.

1436
01:28:16,876 --> 01:28:17,377
Here he goes.

1437
01:28:18,581 --> 01:28:20,746
Oh, what a die for Rosset.

1438
01:28:20,805 --> 01:28:22,390
No, he wanted to get that one in.

1439
01:28:22,890 --> 01:28:23,913
He made a real

1440
01:28:23,894 --> 01:28:29,100
of his second round dive and now he's come out all guns blazing.

1441
01:28:29,121 --> 01:28:30,262
This is the comeback king.

1442
01:28:30,283 --> 01:28:37,091
He's going to absolutely sail above 85 points, buries his entry there, slipping into the water.

1443
01:28:37,612 --> 01:28:39,414
He's hardly throwing up any splash.

1444
01:28:40,115 --> 01:28:40,515
Wow.

1445
01:28:40,796 --> 01:28:43,220
This is the way to get yourself back in contention.

1446
01:28:44,060 --> 01:28:45,243
Am I allowed to hold up a card?

1447
01:28:45,262 --> 01:28:45,963
Say I'm not ready.

1448
01:28:46,064 --> 01:28:46,965
Ask him to do it again.

1449
01:28:47,467 --> 01:28:49,010
No, I don't think you want to do it again.

1450
01:28:49,050 --> 01:28:50,572
That was brilliant.

1451
01:28:50,591 --> 01:28:51,052
87.50.

1452
01:28:51,252 --> 01:28:52,595
It was brilliant.

1453
01:28:52,795 --> 01:28:55,417
And Rossi has really recovered so well.

1454
01:28:55,838 --> 01:28:57,860
Francois Imbeu-Dulac.

1455
01:28:58,601 --> 01:28:59,923
His biggest dive so far.

1456
01:28:59,944 --> 01:29:01,666
3.5 degree of difficulty.

1457
01:29:01,706 --> 01:29:04,890
Reverse three and a half somersaults with tuck.

1458
01:29:04,909 --> 01:29:06,693
He has some work to do to get into the top 18.

1459
01:29:06,712 --> 01:29:08,515
25th of the moment.

1460
01:29:10,621 --> 01:29:12,003
Roy's done well with it.

1461
01:29:12,323 --> 01:29:14,668
Notice there his pre-dive routine.

1462
01:29:14,689 --> 01:29:21,563
He tends to stop there, take a big breath, close his eyes, potentially visualize the dive, and then he sets off.

1463
01:29:21,743 --> 01:29:22,604
Very composed.

1464
01:29:23,206 --> 01:29:26,773
He is a little bit tight to the diving board here, I might add.

1465
01:29:26,752 --> 01:29:27,594
He's okay.

1466
01:29:27,835 --> 01:29:30,118
He turns into a bit of a frog kick as he comes out.

1467
01:29:30,137 --> 01:29:32,462
The breaststrokers would have been pleased with that one.

1468
01:29:32,502 --> 01:29:36,247
Anyway, that's a good dive and it's his highest degree of difficulty.

1469
01:29:37,329 --> 01:29:38,771
Hanging on to the top of his kneecap.

1470
01:29:38,811 --> 01:29:40,614
So look at those frog's legs as he comes out.

1471
01:29:41,136 --> 01:29:41,417
Rabbit.

1472
01:29:45,663 --> 01:29:46,744
That's very unkind.

1473
01:29:47,926 --> 01:29:49,689
We'll start talking about your personage in a moment.

1474
01:29:51,896 --> 01:29:53,921
Now onto Ilya Zakharov.

1475
01:29:54,301 --> 01:29:56,265
This man has been the model of consistency.

1476
01:29:56,426 --> 01:29:59,211
Standby for commentators curse.

1477
01:29:59,230 --> 01:30:02,637
No, he is consistent even with a dodgy takeoff.

1478
01:30:03,560 --> 01:30:05,122
No smiles from the Russian coaches.

1479
01:30:05,863 --> 01:30:14,360
They're here to do business way back from the end of the diving board and I did think that he'd struggle with that but he is superb.

1480
01:30:16,822 --> 01:30:18,685
That can be even better.

1481
01:30:18,704 --> 01:30:26,157
He needs a better hurdle step on his next dive, because he adds another twist to that dive, which goes up to 3.9 degree of difficulty.

1482
01:30:26,197 --> 01:30:27,158
Anyway, we'll tee that out.

1483
01:30:27,177 --> 01:30:27,618
That's 81.

1484
01:30:27,639 --> 01:30:29,582
I can't believe the succession of scores.

1485
01:30:29,601 --> 01:30:31,425
86, 84, 82, 81.

1486
01:30:31,985 --> 01:30:36,653
Just don't get measured up for that.

1487
01:30:40,295 --> 01:30:41,881
Alexander Departee.

1488
01:30:42,846 --> 01:30:48,634
Inward three and a half somersaults with Tuck, the top Canadian, three point four degree of difficulty.

1489
01:30:51,212 --> 01:30:55,979
It's a good dive, little short vertical but this is the dive that Alex hit his head on.

1490
01:30:56,039 --> 01:31:01,608
This is the dive that six weeks ago he smacks his head into the springboard.

1491
01:31:02,269 --> 01:31:11,060
It would have been about this point that he would have connected with the diving board and scalped himself 21 stitches on his forehead and he's here today

1492
01:31:12,104 --> 01:31:19,256
six weeks later showing true courage and true class and he's still in the hunt to make it through.

1493
01:31:19,536 --> 01:31:21,538
Not enjoying it today but he'll get through.

1494
01:31:21,779 --> 01:31:22,400
He'll get through.

1495
01:31:22,640 --> 01:31:23,703
You can tell he's not enjoying it.

1496
01:31:23,922 --> 01:31:27,349
Look on his face tells you that when he's uh on top of his game.

1497
01:31:27,368 --> 01:31:35,462
He's all smiles and waves but today it's uh just get the job done.

1498
01:31:37,449 --> 01:31:40,957
Oh, the Ukrainians rocking and rolling alongside the Russians.

1499
01:31:41,980 --> 01:31:44,768
They've got some big, big dives.

1500
01:31:45,088 --> 01:31:45,810
All of them have.

1501
01:31:46,051 --> 01:31:53,569
They are busting it out today and yeah, nowhere to hide and everyone needs to keep up with them.

1502
01:31:53,548 --> 01:31:58,614
Well, I wonder if they can hold this consistency throughout the prelims and the semis and into the final.

1503
01:31:58,635 --> 01:32:00,237
Of course, the scores do not carry.

1504
01:32:00,317 --> 01:32:05,984
So, whatever the divers do today, it's about shuffling the pack and earning a berth into the semifinals.

1505
01:32:06,345 --> 01:32:06,965
Russia won.

1506
01:32:07,386 --> 01:32:13,412
Ukraine three at the moment in terms of the pecking order with China in second with her charm.

1507
01:32:14,635 --> 01:32:21,462
Uh via Castaneda of Columbia.

1508
01:32:21,443 --> 01:32:23,506
It's a big dive.

1509
01:32:24,707 --> 01:32:25,528
Really big dive.

1510
01:32:25,547 --> 01:32:30,595
Standing backwards, it's 3.5 because you don't get the hurdle step to assist you as you do on the reverse three and a half.

1511
01:32:30,614 --> 01:32:32,898
This is a standing start, if you will.

1512
01:32:34,000 --> 01:32:35,421
Wow, he does very well there.

1513
01:32:35,502 --> 01:32:38,386
Squeezes in, runs out of room a little bit.

1514
01:32:39,567 --> 01:32:40,467
Well, I'm very impressed.

1515
01:32:40,488 --> 01:32:40,908
That's good.

1516
01:32:40,929 --> 01:32:43,292
He's got some big degrees of difficulty coming up.

1517
01:32:45,774 --> 01:32:47,738
Now, what do the judges have to say about that?

1518
01:32:49,506 --> 01:32:51,368
Coach wants to give him a bit of a cuddle already.

1519
01:32:51,389 --> 01:32:55,875
68.25 is his total marks.

1520
01:32:55,954 --> 01:32:59,599
Well, you might have guessed, the first of the two Brits.

1521
01:32:59,618 --> 01:33:05,707
Here's Chris Mears standing on the three-meter springboard, waiting to perform.

1522
01:33:06,127 --> 01:33:11,153
Here's a forward two-and-a-half somersaults with two twists, the most consistent of the two Britons today.

1523
01:33:11,172 --> 01:33:15,918
21st at the moment.

1524
01:33:17,400 --> 01:33:20,904
Oh, it's a decisive dive, and he's nailed it when he needed to.

1525
01:33:22,127 --> 01:33:24,770
Yeah, Tom likes it, and I agree with Tom Daley.

1526
01:33:24,930 --> 01:33:26,152
It's a good dive for Mears.

1527
01:33:26,792 --> 01:33:29,336
Fourth round needed to be good.

1528
01:33:29,416 --> 01:33:35,283
Attacks it out into the double twist, down into the pike, ripping that entry.

1529
01:33:35,304 --> 01:33:40,890
That's it, back in contention, maybe even back in that all-important top 18.

1530
01:33:42,592 --> 01:33:44,234
Super slow motion.

1531
01:33:45,311 --> 01:33:47,416
Can't even keep up with it in slow motion, can we?

1532
01:33:47,536 --> 01:33:48,277
No, it's great.

1533
01:33:49,458 --> 01:33:50,020
Really great.

1534
01:33:50,039 --> 01:33:50,600
Well done, Chris.

1535
01:33:51,042 --> 01:33:51,523
Good stuff.

1536
01:33:52,545 --> 01:33:53,987
Eights across the board.

1537
01:33:54,628 --> 01:33:58,074
Eighty one point six zero and it's giving himself a really good chance now with that.

1538
01:33:58,836 --> 01:34:00,158
It's two more rounds still to go.

1539
01:34:00,198 --> 01:34:06,729
As we look at the former Chinese now Malaysian going for a reverse three and a half somersaults with tuck.

1540
01:34:08,346 --> 01:34:11,091
Oh, he's done years and years and years of training.

1541
01:34:11,752 --> 01:34:17,662
He does look a little bit, well he doesn't quite look as sharp as he used to in his younger days.

1542
01:34:18,524 --> 01:34:27,859
Here we are, reverse three and a half, 30 years old, squeezing into that tuck shake, popping his feet up, just needed to be a little bit higher for that rip entry into the water.

1543
01:34:28,239 --> 01:34:34,911
It'll get over 75 points though and it'll certainly keep him in the mix for a semi-final spot, easily actually.

1544
01:34:36,240 --> 01:34:40,028
77 for Jack Wong.

1545
01:34:41,189 --> 01:34:49,404
Now Jack Law, you know, as you look around and take up the plaudits of the crowd, you have some work to do here.

1546
01:34:49,666 --> 01:34:57,921
Laddie, 17 years of age, a star in Harrogate, European junior champion just a few years ago for three and a half somersault.

1547
01:34:57,940 --> 01:34:59,143
This needs to be good.

1548
01:35:02,042 --> 01:35:05,372
Oh, he's just maybe feeling the pressure.

1549
01:35:05,412 --> 01:35:06,574
It needs to be better than that.

1550
01:35:06,695 --> 01:35:07,417
Come on, Jack.

1551
01:35:07,757 --> 01:35:11,148
You're double world junior champion, double junior European champion.

1552
01:35:11,188 --> 01:35:13,474
You've been in these senior competitions.

1553
01:35:13,493 --> 01:35:17,283
Now you are the youngest competitor and there's more to come.

1554
01:35:17,264 --> 01:35:18,865
more to come from this young man.

1555
01:35:18,905 --> 01:35:21,307
He's not going to move up the field with this.

1556
01:35:21,707 --> 01:35:23,990
This is going to keep him outside the top eighteen.

1557
01:35:24,011 --> 01:35:29,655
That's going to put a lot of pressure on his two dives to come but I'm confident that he can respond.

1558
01:35:29,775 --> 01:35:30,356
Do you know what?

1559
01:35:30,377 --> 01:35:34,541
I think I look on the face of Jack tells you really all you need to know at this stage.

1560
01:35:34,961 --> 01:35:39,185
I think he thinks like we're starting to think that perhaps he's not going to be returning tomorrow.

1561
01:35:39,204 --> 01:35:40,105
I hope that's not the case.

1562
01:35:40,145 --> 01:35:43,069
No, he will be.

1563
01:35:44,229 --> 01:35:47,796
Nineteenth place after a really, really poor start.

1564
01:35:47,817 --> 01:35:51,663
He's done a good reparation job, not quite complete though yet.

1565
01:35:52,444 --> 01:35:56,833
In with three and a half somersaults with tuck, three point four degree of difficulty.

1566
01:35:56,854 --> 01:36:00,180
He's in 19th place after round three.

1567
01:36:02,219 --> 01:36:03,301
Oh, here you go.

1568
01:36:03,841 --> 01:36:09,869
You're going to up the degree of difficulty, increase the risk, and obviously increase the probability of error.

1569
01:36:10,149 --> 01:36:20,145
And that's what we see here from the young diver of Greece, squeezes into the touch shape, just stays in it too long, and lands in a forward roll position.

1570
01:36:21,086 --> 01:36:23,890
Yeah, over he goes, and down the marks go.

1571
01:36:25,675 --> 01:36:27,096
Hm, what a shame.

1572
01:36:27,497 --> 01:36:33,648
What a shame because he was doing so well, but not going to miss to found us his day, I'm afraid, with those marks.

